  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 154 AM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nTropical Storm Bertha, a sheared storm, will continue to move\nslowly west along the Gulf Coast over the next few days. No\nsignificant impacts are expected in our forecast area as it passes\nto the south, but winds will be a little breezy from the north\nWednesday into Thursday.\n\nA robust upper-level ridge centered over the Southern High Plains\nis reinforcing the dry, hot conditions over our region meanwhile.\nA cool front sagging into the region by Wednesday will serve as a\nfocus for afternoon shower and thunderstorm development for the\nback half of the week and next weekend.\n\nConfidence is high for dangerous heat stress conditions to\ncontinue across the area through Wednesday. A mix of Excessive\nHeat Warnings and Heat Advisories will cover the 105+ heat index\nvalues through then. By Thursday, rain chances and the proximity\nof the frontal boundary in the region make hazardous heat less\ncertain for Thursday or later at this time. /NF/",
